Z||000004||ray b||09-04-2001||11:44 AM||||rear anti-roll bar factory stock unit, only ws6 had them. stiffer springs???the sept parts are the same other than shocks that should be gone by now anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||09-04-2001||12:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>rear anti-roll bar factory stock unit, only ws6 had them. stiffer springs???the sept parts are the same other than shocks that should be gone by now anyway.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is wrong. The only cars to have a rear sway bar were the 88 GT and Formula. Both are WS6)<BR>Generally if it's a GT it has the WS6 suspension. This is not always the case with the SE's. The 84/85 SE's and the 84 Indy were all WS6. The 86/87 SE's stock had the Y99 "Rally Tuned Susupension" and WS6 was an option. On the 86/87 SE's you could tell by tires. Y99 had 195/70R14's and WS6 had 215/60R14's. Lots of people put the 215/60R14's on the tech wheels so what the car has on it now is not an indication. The difference between the RTS Y99 and the WS6 were the spring rates.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000006||ray b||09-04-2001||02:00 PM||||wrong no, incomplete maybe,the OE tyre size maybe on the door plate with gvw ect.<BR>but were the shocks the same speck on ws6 cars? what spring letter code is ws6 only?<BR>if it ain't a 88 it ain't going to handle that good anyway. and on the 88 it is eazy to spot the rear bar. any 88 4cyl with ws6?<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||09-04-2001||02:28 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>wrong no, incomplete maybe,the OE tyre size maybe on the door plate with gvw ect.<BR>but were the shocks the same speck on ws6 cars? what spring letter code is ws6 only?<BR>if it ain't a 88 it ain't going to handle that good anyway. and on the 88 it is eazy to spot the rear bar. any 88 4cyl with ws6?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You were wrong, (or do you prefer incorrect) First the rear sway was only 88 but all other years had WS6. Second shocks and struts had nothing to do with WS6. Only the springs. Shocks and struts were the same. There are 4 spring codes listed in the RPO sheet. One code for each spring. What the hell is this "If it ain't an 88 it ain't going to handle" crap. The 84-87 Fiero's handle great. The 88 handled better than 84-87 by eliminating bump steer and the changing the scrub, but that doesn't mean the earlier ones are bad. With minor upgrades and low cost the 84-87 can be made to out-handle a stock 88. <BR>I don't think WS6 was an option on any base coupe. <P>Here is a list of all the RPO codes:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/options.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/options.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||ray b||09-04-2001||04:02 PM||||no shock up grade in ws6??? thats too bad!!!<BR>y99 are very stiff ride in 87 se i had, hard too think of what stiffer ws6 would be like.ouch!!!!<BR>88's ride and handle better, get over it, or get a 88, stop better too, so they start with better base to up grade from and no pre88 will beat a 88 [with the same $$$ spent to up grade both]<BR>back to springs codes are there ws6 only rates what code are they??? like a b c d letter codes as both my 88's [one coupe with swap v6 and one stock forumla ws6] have the same springs codes in front [C] if i remember correctly. v6 rear is diff but v6 needs stiffer springs anyway for extra weight of motor.<BR>what was wrong in first post incomplete yes wrong NO.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000009||Hank is Here||09-04-2001||04:12 PM||||I may be wrong on this point but didn't the 88 coupes have different front control arms as well. Having to do with the the offset of the different rims.   anyone, am i right or wrong?||||reg||1
Z||000010||rockcrawl||09-04-2001||04:22 PM||||I have a GT that has WS6 spring codes on the RPO sticker, but WS6 is not on the sticker. Is WS6 just not shown when there is a WU2 option?||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfiero||09-04-2001||04:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hank is Here:<BR><B>I may be wrong on this point but didn't the 88 coupes have different front control arms as well. Having to do with the the offset of the different rims.   anyone, am i right or wrong?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>All '88 suspension componenets are the same and, therefore interchangeable.<P>The '88 coupes have softer front springs than the Formula or GT, but the rears were almost always the same.<P>'88 coupe front springs are generally ARC and Formulas and '88 GT's are generally ARD.......almost all '88 Fieros have PUC rear springs.<P>Some GT's and Formulas had stiffer front springs.  My 16K mile GT has FPH front springs.<P>I do believe that the shocks and struts were different from the coupes to the Formula/GT......maybe the WS6 cars got gas charged and the base coupes didn't......who knows?<P>I have also heard that the bushings used on WS6 cars were harder, but again, I have no idea.<P>The steering ratios might have been tighter on early WS6 cars too.<P>At any rate.....my knowledge is on '88 Fieros, so I don't know a lot about the early ones.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||ray b||09-04-2001||06:36 PM||||one end or the other were both 'c'thanks mrf<BR>hard bushings makes cents but are they listed as differnt part#??? or build codes??<BR>but are the pre88 cars with y99 code same as ws6 or is there a differt spring rate/code for the ws6?||||reg||1
Z||000013||JJ-85-2M6||09-04-2001||07:19 PM||||In 1985 anyway, the WS6 was standard on GT's and an option on SE's.  You had to order it with a couple other items as well, I think.  The SE's came standard with Y99.  The WS6 cost about 180.00 itself.  I've had 2 1985 2m6 SE's: one with Y99 and the other Ws6.  I don't notice much differnce in handling. Tire size is different.  My Y99 at 80,000 miles actually rides a little less jarringly than my former (new then) WS6 did. J||||reg||1
Z||000014||rockcrawl||09-04-2001||07:38 PM||||For a list of all the different spring codes check this link. <A HREF="http://www.thefieroclub.net/osg/fiero_osg/springs.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thefieroclub.net/osg/fiero_osg/springs.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||ray b||09-04-2001||07:42 PM||||i am sure the 225x50x15's f/r didn't help the ride any on the se but is ws6 mostly wheels and tyres in pre88 cars then?<BR>are you sure about the shocks/rubbers aren't HD in ws6 mr o .<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000016||MrPBody||09-04-2001||09:47 PM||||Also, I think pre-'88 WS6 cars had quicker steering racks -- 3-turn lock-to-lock <I>vs.</I> 3-1/2-turn.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Oreif||09-04-2001||09:59 PM||||Shocks and bushings are the same part number for all years and all models according to the P22 book. All steering racks are the same part number too. The 88's have more turns because with the offset they turned more. WS6 on the earlier cars were tires and springs.<P>rayb, I never said the 88 wasn't better, I just said the pre-88's didn't handle as bad as you make it sound.  ||||reg||1
Z||000018||ray b||09-04-2001||10:32 PM||||corner ok dry but wet the 87 's twitch and spin ez er but diff in ride, 88 much softer, is much more noticeable while no loss in dry feel or speed. rear bar may be most of diff but not all.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000019||cadaver||09-04-2001||11:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>corner ok dry but wet the 87 's twitch and spin ez er but diff in ride, 88 much softer, is much more noticeable while no loss in dry feel or speed. rear bar may be most of diff but not all.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"ez er"??? Oh easier. <BR>"diff" ???Differ or Difference.<BR> Someone needs to gets him self an edjumacation.<BR>So I guess all us non 88 owners should just scrap out cars as they all handle for crapp.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Oreif||09-05-2001||12:16 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>corner ok dry but wet the 87 's twitch and spin ez er but diff in ride, 88 much softer, is much more noticeable while no loss in dry feel or speed. rear bar may be most of diff but not all.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Corner OK? Have you ever driven an earlier Fiero? Sounds like you drove an 87 with bad/cheap tires on it. If it felt "twitch" in the rain, Your tires sucked not the suspension. I have driven many Fiero's and although the 88's had advantages, I prefer the earlier ones. The 88's may feel softer but my preference is a firm/hard ride. <BR>Like you say any suspension can be upgraded. <BR>Mine is tuned to handle a specific way and will out handle/corner many cars easily.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||GT-maniac||09-05-2001||03:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>  Corner OK? Have you ever driven an earlier Fiero? Sounds like you drove an 87 with bad/cheap tires on it. If it felt "twitch" in the rain, Your tires sucked not the suspension. I have driven many Fiero's and although the 88's had advantages, I prefer the earlier ones. The 88's may feel softer but my preference is a firm/hard ride. <BR>Like you say any suspension can be upgraded. <BR>Mine is tuned to handle a specific way and will out handle/corner many cars easily.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-05-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have to agree with Orief here after my recent autocrossing race I'm really beginning to wonder about the much vaunted 88 improved suspension. Both my 85 GT and an 86 SE were competing against an 88 GT and his times weren't any better than ours were and we were all running All Season performance tires. Though I guess a truer test would be to have the same driver run the course in both cars and see if one was quicker with the improved suspension. I'm not saying I wouldn't love to have that suspension but like Orief says that doesn't mean all the earlier cars handle worth a crap. I'm sure we'll get lots of flames from the 88 owners, though if we only had 88 owners on here this sure would be a lonely place.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg"> <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project||||reg||1
Z||000022||Mickey_Moose||09-05-2001||11:03 AM||||Thanks for the info...I didn't really mean to make this into a heated debate about which is better  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>myself having drive both, 88 seems stiffer (or at least mine does compared to others), but the earlier one also steered a fair bit easier. Over all the 88 seemed to be stiff all around (steering, braking, gas pedal) - not saying it's better, just what I noticed - would all depend on what you like.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000023||chester||09-05-2001||11:34 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadaver:<BR><B> "ez er"??? Oh easier. <BR>"diff" ???Differ or Difference.<BR> Someone needs to gets him self an edjumacation.<BR>So I guess all us non 88 owners should just scrap out cars as they all handle for crapp.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ROFLMAO!  Yeah I guess so.  All you scrapping your cars let me know.  I want them CHEAP!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I guess some are just learning them their letters.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">    <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
